, 2019), since the rule and staff guidance may have changed by November 2026.\n\nWith reasonable confidence, the rule exempts qualifying ETFs from certain Investment Company Act provisions, including the redemption and resale-price provisions of Sections 22(d) and 22(e), subject to conditions addressing:\n\n- **Affiliate limits:** restrictions on affiliated persons acting as authorized participants or otherwise influencing creation and redemption baskets.\n- **Custom baskets:** written policies and procedures keeping basket construction consistent and non-discriminatory.\n- **Foreign investments:** later settlement of creations and redemptions where local market settlement requires it, with timing conditions.\n\nFor exact conditions and thresholds, consult the rule text or counsel.","ttft_ms":2324,"type":"result","duration_ms":3355,"uuid":"5a36de21-f59b-42dd-bb15-90e9acd5537f","ttft_stream_ms":452,"time_to_request_ms":57,"first_content_frame_ms":452,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"credential_expires_at":"2026-11-28T06:36:39.484Z"}
